The person must have built fintech or travel products before, not operated them.
Title:- Product Manager / Senior Product Manager Travel Fintech Location- Gurugram Experience- 4-10 years total, with at least 3 years as a PM in travel fintech, payments, or travel tech Who we're looking for This role is open only to product managers whose PM experience comes from one of these backgrounds: Travel fintech / B2B travel payments virtual cards for travel, travel BNPL, B2B travel wallets, airline/hotel payment and settlement platforms Spend management & corporate card fintechs — corporate cards, expense management, T&E platforms OTAs and TMCs — in the payments, wallet, checkout, refunds or finance-product team Travel tech companies — owning payments, billing, invoicing or settlement modules The experience must be in a product management role (owning roadmap, writing PRDs, shipping with engineering).
At least part of it must involve travel.
Must-have 3+ years as a Product Manager in travel fintech, spend management, or the payments team of an OTA, TMC or travel tech company Shipped at least one payments or card product to live customers, and can walk through it end to end Solid grasp of card issuing: issuer, processor, program manager and network roles;
virtual cards Understanding of travel money flows: BSP/ARC settlement, airline and hotel payment terms, refunds and reissues, the TMC billing model Experience with KYB/KYC, AML basics and working with compliance or banking partners Can read API docs and discuss payment request/response flows, webhooks and idempotency with engineers Strong PRD writing and user flows;
able to present to client CFOs and finance teams Nice to have Built for both India and the UAE/GCC (RBI PPI/card rules, CBUAE, UPI, local acquirers) Expense management: receipt OCR, GST/VAT input credit, per diems, ERP sync (SAP, Oracle, Tally, Zoho) Experience with B2B travel payment providers or virtual card programs for travel suppliers Fraud and risk rules engines, dispute and chargeback workflows AI features in finance: auto-categorisation, anomaly detection, policy agents SQL or analytics tools for spend and funnel analysis Not a fit Please do not apply if your background is mainly any of the following: Payment operations, reconciliation, settlement or finance operations Chargeback, dispute or collections handling Travel operations, ticketing, fulfilment or back office Customer support, onboarding support or account management Banking relationship, sales or partnerships roles without product ownership Product roles in consumer lending, insurance or retail payments with no B2B or travel exposure Business analyst or project manager roles with no roadmap or PRD ownership

